#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179547 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179688 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "78adaeaa-a91e-53e2-a192-1440d4d41211" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Divergence of a Vector Field Using Linearity Properties"}] :question/id #uuid "bb7ae99a-b8d9-5e4d-906c-9e18d22c1404" :question/math-academy-id "e-8742" :question/problem "Calculate $\\nabla \\cdot (\\mathbf{F}-3\\mathbf{G})$ for the vector fields $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G,$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}=\\left(x^2+y\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i}+ \\left(xy-y^2\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}, \\quad \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{G}=x+y.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf F$ and $\\mathbf G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $\\nabla \\cdot (k \\mathbf F) = k \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf F$\n\n- $\\nabla \\cdot (\\mathbf F + \\mathbf G) = \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf F + \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-3G) & =∇\\cdot (F)+∇\\cdot (-3G) \\\\  & =∇\\cdot F-3∇\\cdot G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{F}.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2x+x-2y \\\\  & =3x-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F-3G) & =∇\\cdot F-3∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =(3x-2y)-3\\cdot (x+y) \\\\  & =-5y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179549 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179690 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "44d953c5-21bb-5326-bfac-e793cfe26cd2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Divergence of a Vector Field Using the Product Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "7de054d4-8384-5aab-b2c4-a43b1f86a16c" :question/math-academy-id "e-8928" :question/problem "Given that $\\mathbf F(x,y) = \\left\\langle \\dfrac 1x, xy \\right \\rangle$ and $f(x,y) = \\dfrac 1{x},$ calculate $\\nabla \\cdot (f\\,\\mathbf F).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\nabla \\cdot (f\\,\\mathbf F) = f\\, \\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf {F}+  \\mathbf F \\cdot \\nabla f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf {F}$ and $\\nabla f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},0⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{x})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+x)+⟨\\frac{1}{x},xy⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},0⟩ \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241097 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179688 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "78adaeaa-a91e-53e2-a192-1440d4d41211" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Divergence of a Vector Field Using Linearity Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09dc01da-2660-5cdf-b0fa-a152d2942087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238151} {:answer/id #uuid "2242969b-860c-5835-8b35-57367aa4ec32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2y(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238355} {:answer/id #uuid "29cd6443-9f90-57f0-9bcb-d96c14b03760" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238423} {:answer/id #uuid "dfa03014-6326-5bd2-b5a3-a79fc531fc0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240008} {:answer/id #uuid "f3596578-6003-586e-b0bb-695d533cd500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09dc01da-2660-5cdf-b0fa-a152d2942087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238151} :answer-field/id #uuid "9aa9dd5a-693f-5e97-aa2d-7ed5edc6f040" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240598}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9703f536-70eb-5a05-8c4a-7f2c7607a6b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-105642" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\cdot (F+G)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,i-{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,j,\\,∇\\cdot G=2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)) \\\\  & =-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\  & =-4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F+G) & =∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =-4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\  & =-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366850 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179690 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "44d953c5-21bb-5326-bfac-e793cfe26cd2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Divergence of a Vector Field Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e772d5fd-8873-5f01-8e0e-9b2d188dbee8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}(3y+2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366852} {:answer/id #uuid "0749c0e0-86d1-5ce9-bc17-1a82f5495ba5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy(xy+2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366853} {:answer/id #uuid "daa2a4aa-b4aa-539e-bf61-98bbcc57db7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}y(3y+4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366854} {:answer/id #uuid "a400b6c4-fad3-550e-9c64-998d075118a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}y(y+2x+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366855} {:answer/id #uuid "f322dbbd-44f7-50d7-97ec-555e953573ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}(3{y}^{2}+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "daa2a4aa-b4aa-539e-bf61-98bbcc57db7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}y(3y+4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366854} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5db2c67-62b4-5732-b4f3-224a2f67e30c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366851}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf849e13-e8f1-55b6-b51f-70bad727cc07" :question/math-academy-id "q-105743" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y)=⟨xy,2y⟩$ and $f(x,y)={x}^{2}y,$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨2xy,{x}^{2}⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y)=y+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & ={x}^{2}y(y+2)+⟨xy,2y⟩\\cdot ⟨2xy,{x}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{y}^{2}+2{x}^{2}y+2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+2{x}^{2}y \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+4{x}^{2}y \\\\  & ={x}^{2}y(3y+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367366 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179688 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "78adaeaa-a91e-53e2-a192-1440d4d41211" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Divergence of a Vector Field Using Linearity Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81140528-55a2-55ee-a446-c4ecc4c389dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x{y}^{2}+2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367368} {:answer/id #uuid "4d99e938-b77d-5e49-9ef0-2b8dd93510e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367369} {:answer/id #uuid "eaf7538b-e8be-53f6-845e-acbc84a6dd44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy-y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367370} {:answer/id #uuid "a76b0d37-e266-5f23-bb84-9c2088fc0784" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xy+3y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367371} {:answer/id #uuid "50aebbec-bc0b-570c-b51a-a4d30ffaac7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{y}^{3}-y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50aebbec-bc0b-570c-b51a-a4d30ffaac7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{y}^{3}-y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367372} :answer-field/id #uuid "f51dbd77-8136-52af-a21a-6a5b89bd8649" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8e4f4f05-cab9-5b00-b80d-9d3be44e8ac8" :question/math-academy-id "q-131245" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}F+4G)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF={x}^{2}{y}^{3}\\,i+{y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,j,\\,∇\\cdot G=-\\frac{1}{2}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}F+4G) & =∇\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}F)+∇\\cdot (4G) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}∇\\cdot F+4∇\\cdot G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{3})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =2x{y}^{3}+2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}F+2G) & =\\frac{1}{2}∇\\cdot F+4∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2x{y}^{3}+2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+4\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =x{y}^{3}+y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =x{y}^{3}-y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266067 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179690 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "44d953c5-21bb-5326-bfac-e793cfe26cd2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Divergence of a Vector Field Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08612da6-00e6-5565-b1b4-b002ee6d449d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(xy-1){e}^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263077} {:answer/id #uuid "185d2e60-1d02-5e5d-a588-c3af72c99d02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(y-1){e}^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263230} {:answer/id #uuid "3ebce6aa-c045-5bdb-b341-49efe839fc91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(3y+1){e}^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263554} {:answer/id #uuid "6d086b17-e4d8-5e48-b924-63b0d3ebeb7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(y+1){e}^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263943} {:answer/id #uuid "fa628dc9-f28d-5e80-8945-778ac8830569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x({y}^{2}+x){e}^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ebce6aa-c045-5bdb-b341-49efe839fc91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(3y+1){e}^{y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263554} :answer-field/id #uuid "1afd5b7a-e97d-5670-86ec-c6252b479311" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "850b167e-fac7-553f-bd45-68edd2f03d28" :question/math-academy-id "q-131288" :question/problem "Given that $F(x,y)=⟨xy,y⟩$ and $f(x,y)=x{e}^{y},$ calculate $∇\\cdot (f\\,F).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\cdot (f\\,F)=f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇\\cdot F$ and $∇f.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f & =⟨{e}^{y},x{e}^{y}⟩, \\\\ ∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y)=y+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (f\\,F) & =f\\,∇\\cdot F+F\\cdot ∇f \\\\  & =x{e}^{y}(y+1)+⟨xy,y⟩\\cdot ⟨{e}^{y},x{e}^{y}⟩ \\\\  & =xy{e}^{y}+x{e}^{y}+xy{e}^{y}+xy{e}^{y} \\\\  & =3xy{e}^{y}+x{e}^{y} \\\\  & =x(3y+1){e}^{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180185 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179688 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "78adaeaa-a91e-53e2-a192-1440d4d41211" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Divergence of a Vector Field Using Linearity Properties"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a725a9b2-05ff-5f46-a6f0-13300530fe31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2(1 + x))/(y^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178655} {:answer/id #uuid "cb7e3346-b9e6-54c2-b6fd-5b20ee998dba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2(1 + xy))/(y^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178656} {:answer/id #uuid "eaf44999-8b29-5ee5-9e4c-9acb45278ad1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178657} {:answer/id #uuid "1e2654d3-2c50-5132-ad53-44347c77a0c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2(1 + y))/(y^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178658} {:answer/id #uuid "5a567331-c377-55a2-8301-311afa5ead8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x}{y^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178659}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ab0653b7-142b-5287-afed-0531b2d699e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186178654} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f355aca-d71f-57d0-ad5b-f6b4c1c3ee42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(1+y)}{{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368549} {:answer/id #uuid "52387e5c-65fa-59b4-b443-c7ae60751678" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368550} {:answer/id #uuid "9e2acff5-dcff-581e-8504-084584b55f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(1+xy)}{{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368551} {:answer/id #uuid "b5eb34bb-be52-5af3-b44b-0163802a7ebd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368552} {:answer/id #uuid "63cf6f6e-7586-5d2d-965e-6a5a468c7dd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(1+x)}{{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f355aca-d71f-57d0-ad5b-f6b4c1c3ee42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(1+y)}{{y}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368549} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d6b9ea4-bc00-5b64-9f13-831ea284d323" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d98d41c-4aeb-5c37-80bb-0d675e8879ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-41842" :question/problem "Calculate $∇\\cdot (F+2G)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡{y}^{2}\\,j,\\,∇\\cdot G=-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $∇\\cdot (kF)=k∇\\cdot F$\n\n- $∇\\cdot (F+G)=∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot G.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F+2G) & =∇\\cdot F+∇\\cdot (2G) \\\\  & =∇\\cdot F+2∇\\cdot G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}))+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{2y}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot (F+2G) & =∇\\cdot F+2∇\\cdot G \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{y}+2\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{y}-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{y}+\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{{y}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1+y)}{{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180310 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179690 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "44d953c5-21bb-5326-bfac-e793cfe26cd2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Divergence of a Vector Field Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b71972ff-94fd-53dd-a621-a3b7602062e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy(1 + xy)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179405} {:answer/id #uuid "eefba093-5bdf-5507-9f65-0c0d071a4bf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy(1 + y^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179406} {:answer/id #uuid "41a9f352-4737-5c30-828b-ca93c09f8738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy(1 + y^{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179407} {:answer/id #uuid "6aaeed13-7bd4-50dc-89f0-843d3a1ef68a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy(1 + x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179408} {:answer/id #uuid "764ccee6-29f3-5e70-87e2-37db1bd7cb3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2xy(1 + x^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179409}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9c37c60e-e97b-5fd7-8819-529b45993a1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179404}] :question/id #uuid "